.TH SPRITEPUT 1
.SH NAME
spriteput \- sprites stored in the source file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/spriteput
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I SpritePut
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/SpritePut.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
The US flag three times and the US map once, which is what the original
prints.  The point is where the pictures live: the binary sprite sits in
the source file after the text, addressed by a bin number, and
.B $SP,"",BI=1$
is the placeholder the editor shows in text mode.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B "any key"
Exit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/spriteput.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR spriteedit (1),
.IR wm (1)
